      "message": "Splitting method allow to easily identify which part of the code is behind a flag from which one is not.\n\nBelow suggestion add a flag, split the method and also doing early return to prevent having extra identation and having the if far away from the error check\n\n```suggestion\nstatic tGATT_STATUS _proc_write_req_flagged(tGATT_WRITE_REQ* p_data,\n                                         uint16_t conn_id) {\n  for (const auto\u0026 db_addr : gatt_attr) {\n    if (p_data-\u003ehandle !\u003d db_addr.handle) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (db_addr.uuid !\u003d GATT_UUID_CHAR_CLIENT_CONFIG) {\n      return GATT_WRITE_NOT_PERMIT;\n    }\n    uint8_t value \u003d 0;\n    uint8_t* p \u003d p_data-\u003evalue;\n    STREAM_TO_UINT8(value, p);\n\n    tGATT_TCB\u0026 tcb \u003d gatt_cb.tcb[GATT_GET_TCB_IDX(conn_id)];\n    btif_storage_set_encr_data_cccd(tcb.peer_bda, value);\n    return GATT_SUCCESS;\n  }\n  return GATT_NOT_FOUND;\n}\n\ntGATT_STATUS proc_write_req(tGATTS_REQ_TYPE, tGATT_WRITE_REQ* p_data,\n                            uint16_t conn_id) {\n  if (IS_FLAG_ENABLED(encrypted_advertising_data)) {\n    return _proc_write_req_flagged(p_data, conn_id);\n  }\n  for (const auto\u0026 db_addr : gatt_attr)\n    if (p_data-\u003ehandle \u003d\u003d db_addr.handle) return GATT_WRITE_NOT_PERMIT;\n\n  return GATT_NOT_FOUND;\n}\n```\n\nLet me know if you think this does not need to be flag (and why) as there may be reason not to flag in some cases",
